/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  flash13_acetic_ethanol_vacuum_flash -- the reactive flash that FLASHES.

  flash12's chemistry with a volatile-rich feed (12 % ethanol) pulled under
  vacuum: at 358.15 K / 0.65 atm the two-phase reactive slice solves the
  COUPLED system -- speciation + electroneutrality + gas-liquid transfer +
  the acetic vapour DIMER re-weighting the vapour mole balance (apparent
  moles = n_mono + 2 n_dim) + ethanol's authorised ideal Raoult leg -- in
  one Newton over (ln V, vapour-odds), 13 iterations, quadratic tail.

  What the student sees: V/F = 0.415; ethanol enriches into the vapour
  (y = 0.169 vs x_feed = 0.12); the BUFFER HOLDS THE AMMONIA -- 99.97 % of
  the NH3 stays in the liquid as NH4+ (y_NH3 = 3e-4) while the molecular
  acid escapes and the liquid pH rises 4.62 -> 4.88; the vapour dimer share
  is 12 % and its association heat (-0.74 kW) is priced EXACTLY into the
  duty (h_dim = 2 h_mono + dH).  Sum of vapour partials = P identically.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

application   choupoSolve;
description  "Reactive VACUUM flash, two-phase: V/F = 0.42 at 358.15 K / 0.65 atm -- ethanol strips, the buffer holds the ammonia (y_NH3 = 3e-4), dimer re-weights the vapour balance, association heat priced";
verbosity     3;

reports
{
    streamTable    { }
    massBalance    { }
}
